workplan/2026-10-30-ramp-spec-pages/RENDER-CONTRACT-parameters-3-and-12.md:15:**Relation to `RENDER-DECISIONS-AND-PIPELINE.md`.** Another session, working in parallel, recorded the owner's render decisions of 2026-10-29/30 in the ledger ("Owner rulings 2026-10-30", and its second entry) and wrote a first-pass element table (its section 3, from `PRAGMA table_info`). This contract is the probe-backed, adversarially reviewed version of that table for parameters 3 and 12 and is to be read with those rulings: best practice names the most accommodating value found (the ledger's item 1, with the ○ band and flag kept); the page offers an audience lens and a disability lens (item 4); rows with no value are not shown and the Gaps section states them (item 9a). Where its section 3 and this file differ for these two parameters, this file is the more recent.
workplan/2026-10-30-ramp-spec-pages/RENDER-CONTRACT-parameters-3-and-12.md:30:- **C9. Voice: describe and attribute; do not adjudicate a correct path.** The guidebook's own voice says what a source states, where, and in what state ("the Irish Technical Guidance Document M, 2022, Table 2, states ..."). It does not say a value is correct, safe or adequate, and it uses no "should" or "must" of its own; a source's "should" or "must" is quoted as the source's. **"Best practice" is not banned**: the ratified register map (`governance/evidence-architecture.md` section 6) renders "best practice: X [●]", and the posture DR defines it as the practice the evidence best supports, offered as a figure for thought. It may appear only as that map defines it, with its marker, its derivation and its disagreements in view, never as a bare endorsement. The ledger of 2026-10-30 (item 1 and its second entry) rules that the value named as best practice is the most accommodating one found in the parameter's direction, and that a value resting on T4 to T6 alone keeps the ○ band and the weak, code-derived flag; the phrase stays, under those conditions.
workplan/2026-10-30-ramp-spec-pages/RENDER-CONTRACT-parameters-3-and-12.md:41:| E1 | Hero: what the stated rule derives for each parameter, with the derivation, the strength flag, the marker, the disagreements and the sources it rests on (R1). The rule is named as the guidebook's own choice (OR-4, "the most accommodating value wins"), and the page says that adjudication is the author's judgment, as the posture DR's flagged judgment 1 requires | `specifications`: `state`, `value_min`, `value_max`, `value_unit`, `value_notations`, `marker`, `tier_basis`, `code_floor_only`, `rule_version`, `derivation_sha`; `v_best_practice` (a T6-only cell is to appear flagged ○, OR-7, so T-5 changes its `code_floor_only = 0` filter) | one live row per (parameter, lens) | print the gap (C4); never a number | **BLOCKED.** No live determination. Needs T-2 to T-4 and the first engine run S-1 |
